Bash Notes
---------------

Terminal is a REPL
Read, Eval, Print, Loop

Tab can be used for autocomplete

history command shows terminal session command history

Running /bin/ls as a command works as if using ls

compgen -b shows all commands built into bash

Be mindful that commands in bash might work different than the same commands built onto your system

To run a script without permissions you can do bash ./script.sh

yes command exists and just spams 'y'

